{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string that was encoded using the encode_shift function.\n    Each character is shifted back by 5 positions in the alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        # Calculate the 0-indexed position of the character relative to 'a'\n        shifted_alphabet_index = ord(ch) - ord('a')\n        # Shift back by 5, using modulo 26 to handle wrap-around for negative results\n        original_alphabet_index = (shifted_alphabet_index - 5) % 26\n        # Convert the index back to a character and append\n        decoded_chars.append(chr(original_alphabet_index + ord('a')))\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
