{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Uses trial division, first for 2 and then odd numbers.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer greater than 1\")\n\n    last_factor = None\n\n    # Remove all factors of 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        last_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            last_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be a prime itself\n    if n > 1:\n        last_factor = n\n\n    return last_factor"}
