{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circularly shifts digits of integer x right by shift, returning the result as a string.\n    If shift exceeds the number of digits, the digits are reversed instead.\"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    is_negative = (x < 0)\n    s_digits = str(abs(x))\n    L = len(s_digits)\n\n    # If shift is greater than the number of digits, reverse the digits.\n    if shift > L:\n        reversed_digits = s_digits[::-1]\n        return \"-\" + reversed_digits if is_negative else reversed_digits\n\n    # Normalize shift to be within the range [0, L-1] and positive for right shift.\n    # (shift % L + L) % L handles both positive and negative shifts correctly.\n    effective_shift = (shift % L + L) % L\n\n    # Perform the circular right shift using string slicing.\n    shifted_digits = s_digits[L - effective_shift:] + s_digits[:L - effective_shift]\n\n    return \"-\" + shifted_digits if is_negative else shifted_digits"}
