{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "def check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the last character of a string is an alphabetical letter and forms a standalone token.\n    A token is standalone if preceded by a space or is the string's only character.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not txt:\n        return False\n\n    if txt[-1].isspace():\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    if len(txt) == 1:\n        return True\n\n    prev_char = txt[-2]\n    if prev_char == ' ':\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False"}
