{"task_id": "HumanEval/147", "solution": "def get_max_triples(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given a positive integer n. You have to create an integer array a of length n.\n        For each i (1 \u2264 i \u2264 n), the value of a[i] = i * i - i + 1.\n        Return the number of triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) of a where i < j < k,\n    and a[i] + a[j] + a[k] is a multiple of 3.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates n choose k (C(n, k)).\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    count0 = 0  # Count of a[x] such that a[x] % 3 == 0\n    count1 = 0  # Count of a[x] such that a[x] % 3 == 1\n\n    # Analyze a[i] % 3 based on i % 3:\n    # If i % 3 == 0, then a[i] = i*i - i + 1 => (0*0 - 0 + 1) % 3 = 1 % 3. So a[i] % 3 == 1.\n    # If i % 3 == 1, then a[i] = i*i - i + 1 => (1*1 - 1 + 1) % 3 = 1 % 3. So a[i] % 3 == 1.\n    # If i % 3 == 2, then a[i] = i*i - i + 1 => (2*2 - 2 + 1) % 3 = (4 - 2 + 1) % 3 = 3 % 3. So a[i] % 3 == 0.\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        rem_i = i % 3\n        if rem_i == 0 or rem_i == 1:\n            count1 += 1\n        else:  # rem_i == 2\n            count0 += 1\n\n    # For a[i] + a[j] + a[k] to be divisible by 3, the sum of their remainders modulo 3 must be 0.\n    # The only combinations of (0, 1) remainders that sum to 0 (mod 3) are:\n    # (1, 1, 1) => 1 + 1 + 1 = 3, which is 0 (mod 3)\n    # (0, 0, 0) => 0 + 0 + 0 = 0, which is 0 (mod 3)\n\n    # Calculate the number of ways to choose 3 elements from count1 elements and from count0 elements.\n    total_triples = combinations(count1, 3) + combinations(count0, 3)\n\n    return total_triples"}
